---
// src/pages/about.astro — 100% static page, no island.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="fw × Astro — about">
    <h1>About this example</h1>
    <p>
        Demo of the official <code>@awacloud/fw/astro</code> integration:
        Astro runs on Vite, the integration re-injects the
        <code>@awacloud/fw/vite</code> plugin via the
        <code>astro:config:setup</code> hook, which makes the virtual
        modules <code>virtual:@awacloud/fw/preset/*</code> available
        everywhere — frontmatter (SSR) as well as client scripts.
    </p>
    <h2>Boundaries</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Frontmatter / SSR</strong>: only worker-safe modules
            (<code>render.toHTML</code>, <code>parser</code>,
            codecs, <code>valid</code>…). Never a DOM module.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Client scripts</strong>: the whole preset
            (<code>uiSession</code>, <code>form</code>, <code>signal</code>,
            <code>dom</code>, <code>events</code>…).
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Sanity layer</strong>: <code>sanity: 'community'</code> in
            <code>astro.config.mjs</code> is injected by the integration as a
            <em>client-only</em> script on every page (including this one) —
            never at SSR.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        This page loads no island: Astro ships only static HTML
        (+ the sanity script injected by the integration).
    </p>
</Layout>
